WEBVTT

00:00:00.360 --> 00:00:03.220
What's the problem with that Anima?

00:00:03.220 --> 00:00:05.430
Cracking her allies' comm 
links to shoot them down?

00:00:05.430 --> 00:00:06.680
That's crazy!

00:00:06.680 --> 00:00:09.100
Why did you bring someone like that here?

00:00:09.100 --> 00:00:11.800
Overwhelming skill and talent.

00:00:11.800 --> 00:00:13.230
Combat experience.

00:00:13.840 --> 00:00:17.960
She's at a level that Gripen 
and Eagle can't hope to match.

00:00:18.320 --> 00:00:19.900
Now that the continent's fallen,

00:00:19.900 --> 00:00:23.130
Komatsu is the front line 
of the war. We need her.

00:00:23.130 --> 00:00:26.750
But teamwork will be 
impossible at this rate!

00:00:30.770 --> 00:00:34.960
Do you think she's a bad person?

00:00:35.520 --> 00:00:37.710
Well, I don't think we can trust her.

00:00:37.710 --> 00:00:40.370
I don't understand what she's thinking.

00:00:41.500 --> 00:00:44.470
Then the one thing I can do is 
correct that misunderstanding.

00:00:44.830 --> 00:00:48.170
As for the way she thinks,
 her highest priority...

00:00:48.530 --> 00:00:50.180
...is to save humanity.

00:02:22.990 --> 00:02:26.330
<b>No Smoking</b>

00:02:23.930 --> 00:02:26.320
It's saving humanity from the Xi.

00:02:26.320 --> 00:02:27.310
Listen to me.

00:02:26.870 --> 00:02:31.830
<i>Raison d'Etre</i>

00:02:27.710 --> 00:02:31.150
Not humans. Humanity.

00:02:31.560 --> 00:02:35.410
She's trying to protect the entire species.

00:02:35.410 --> 00:02:37.670
Humanity?

00:02:38.370 --> 00:02:41.530
She's the first Anima the JSDF created.

00:02:42.040 --> 00:02:44.050
She was my first work.

00:02:44.530 --> 00:02:46.320
We had some unusual hopes for her,

00:02:46.320 --> 00:02:49.290
and we didn't know when the 
next Anima would come.

00:02:49.570 --> 00:02:53.360
Perhaps she thought she had 
to do everything by herself.

00:02:54.180 --> 00:02:56.330
You know what Eagle's personality is like.

00:02:56.670 --> 00:02:58.600
There's no way she'll be able 
to get along with Phantom.

00:02:59.000 --> 00:03:02.230
I thought that you and Gripen might...

00:03:02.230 --> 00:03:03.520
I'm sorry.

00:03:03.520 --> 00:03:05.610
That relationship has already fractured.

00:03:07.820 --> 00:03:10.380
Maybe you should all go get drunk together?

00:03:10.380 --> 00:03:11.990
Get to know each other better.

00:03:12.650 --> 00:03:15.250
I'm a minor.

00:03:15.250 --> 00:03:16.830
I'm joking.

00:03:17.840 --> 00:03:22.840
The realistic solution is to limit the 
amount of time you interact with each other.

00:03:23.220 --> 00:03:25.920
But is that really a team, then?

00:03:26.310 --> 00:03:28.270
<b>Director's Office</b>

00:03:32.450 --> 00:03:35.270
Are you done talking with Haruka?

00:03:35.270 --> 00:03:37.070
I guess.

00:03:37.070 --> 00:03:38.840
Want to go get some food?

00:03:38.840 --> 00:03:40.250
I need to talk to you.

00:03:40.730 --> 00:03:42.480
So let's go somewhere quiet.

00:03:43.690 --> 00:03:45.480
Are you okay?

00:03:45.910 --> 00:03:48.210
I'm so hungry, I could die.

00:03:48.210 --> 00:03:49.490
We're going right now!

00:03:57.570 --> 00:03:59.140
Heaven?

00:03:59.140 --> 00:04:01.480
Don't be ridiculous.

00:04:03.330 --> 00:04:05.770
I brought some yogurt drinks.

00:04:05.770 --> 00:04:07.970
I got two. One for me and one for...

00:04:08.350 --> 00:04:10.960
Hey, don't act like I 
brought them both for you!

00:04:13.800 --> 00:04:15.310
Here, eat up.

00:04:15.310 --> 00:04:16.420
Thanks.

00:04:19.180 --> 00:04:20.410
Um...

00:04:21.480 --> 00:04:23.560
Here. "Aah."

00:04:24.230 --> 00:04:26.720
Where did you learn to do that?

00:04:26.720 --> 00:04:31.020
One of the maintenance staff said that 
I could seduce any man by doing this.

00:04:31.340 --> 00:04:33.580
I need to talk to that guy.

00:04:33.580 --> 00:04:35.400
Badly.

00:04:36.480 --> 00:04:37.930
You're not happy?

00:04:38.240 --> 00:04:41.900
You only do stuff like 
that for someone special.

00:04:42.280 --> 00:04:44.880
I think you're special, Kei.

00:04:45.290 --> 00:04:47.580
That's not it.

00:04:47.580 --> 00:04:51.090
I mean, if you like them,
or you're in love...

00:04:51.090 --> 00:04:52.790
I like you Kei.

00:04:52.790 --> 00:04:54.190
I love you.

00:04:54.190 --> 00:04:57.230
Don't say that until you actually 
know what those words mean.

00:05:06.410 --> 00:05:10.120
You girls are all unique, aren't you?

00:05:10.120 --> 00:05:11.460
You mean us Anima?

00:05:11.460 --> 00:05:16.720
You all seem like really 
different people.

00:05:17.460 --> 00:05:22.820
Wouldn't it be easier to just 
make a group of JAS39s

00:05:22.820 --> 00:05:24.660
and a group of F-15s?

00:05:24.660 --> 00:05:26.010
That's impossible.

00:05:26.010 --> 00:05:29.290
You can only make one Anima 
from a particular model.

00:05:29.290 --> 00:05:30.590
Really?

00:05:30.590 --> 00:05:32.790
When Eagle was born,

00:05:32.790 --> 00:05:35.710
it meant the end of all attempts to 
make a Daughter from the F-15 family.

00:05:35.710 --> 00:05:41.080
She's a J model, but there will 
be no C or D models born.

00:05:41.510 --> 00:05:44.950
In the same way that humanity as a 
group has its own survival instincts,

00:05:44.950 --> 00:05:49.850
the "species" called JAS39 and F-15 
have their own unique characters

00:05:49.850 --> 00:05:51.890
and raison d'être.

00:05:51.890 --> 00:05:54.330
And the Anima may be an icon of that.

00:05:54.630 --> 00:05:59.490
It may be that creating a soul isn't so 
simple that you can do it with a single plane.

00:05:59.490 --> 00:06:02.140
That's what someone from TRDI said once.

00:06:02.500 --> 00:06:04.960
That's really philosophical.

00:06:06.130 --> 00:06:10.590
That means that you guys are just 
gonna have to get along, I guess.

00:06:11.720 --> 00:06:13.110
Sorry.

00:06:13.110 --> 00:06:14.930
I'll explain.

00:06:18.520 --> 00:06:20.260
Humanity's salvation...

00:06:21.190 --> 00:06:22.300
Yeah.

00:06:22.300 --> 00:06:24.240
I think I understand that.

00:06:25.390 --> 00:06:27.950
"If I go down, it's all over."

00:06:28.540 --> 00:06:32.860
Just looking at the combat 
information archives tells you

00:06:32.860 --> 00:06:36.250
how much pressure the first 
Daughters were under.

00:06:36.820 --> 00:06:38.700
It's not just Phantom.

00:06:38.700 --> 00:06:41.540
All the Anima in the other countries 
are the same too, probably.

00:06:41.830 --> 00:06:43.210
Other countries?

00:06:43.210 --> 00:06:44.190
That's right.

00:06:44.190 --> 00:06:47.680
Russia was the first country to 
research the Anima and Daughters.

00:06:47.680 --> 00:06:49.600
Next was the Japanese Phantom.

00:06:49.600 --> 00:06:51.560
Then the American Rhino, later.

00:06:52.000 --> 00:06:55.970
But forget that, Kei. We have our 
own problem to deal with!

00:06:56.760 --> 00:06:58.100
What's that?

00:06:58.100 --> 00:07:00.450
We need to be strong enough 
to defend Komatsu Base.

00:07:00.450 --> 00:07:03.480
And so we need to win in one 
of our training exercises.

00:07:03.920 --> 00:07:06.420
We lost to both Eagle and Phantom.

00:07:06.420 --> 00:07:09.580
Right now, we're in last place.
 At the bottom.

00:07:09.580 --> 00:07:11.700
This is a serious emergency.

00:07:12.050 --> 00:07:15.000
Oh, you're right.

00:07:15.000 --> 00:07:17.340
I was supposed to be 
thinking about that, too.

00:07:17.340 --> 00:07:18.160
Yeah.

00:07:28.650 --> 00:07:30.170
I'm so tired.

00:07:30.170 --> 00:07:32.220
I knew we left too late.

00:07:32.220 --> 00:07:34.400
In the end, this was all we got.

00:07:34.880 --> 00:07:37.270
Is this place always like this?

00:07:37.270 --> 00:07:41.080
It's the place with the biggest 
discounts near the station.

00:07:41.080 --> 00:07:44.160
And it's running the biggest 
sale in its history this week.

00:07:44.470 --> 00:07:47.720
You dragged me out of the 
house on my one day off.

00:07:48.280 --> 00:07:51.970
<i>I haven't had any time to think about 
the homework Gripen gave me.</i>

00:07:52.270 --> 00:07:56.840
Don't worry. Big Sis Minghua will treat you 
to something as thanks for your hard work!

00:07:56.840 --> 00:07:58.960
Anything you want!

00:07:58.960 --> 00:08:00.540
Seriously?

00:08:00.540 --> 00:08:02.470
I-In exchange...

00:08:02.470 --> 00:08:04.810
Come with me this afternoon.

00:08:04.810 --> 00:08:07.360
There's a new supermarket near the station.

00:08:07.360 --> 00:08:09.760
We can get things there we couldn't get here.

00:08:08.210 --> 00:08:10.030
Yes? Hello?

00:08:10.460 --> 00:08:13.800
<i>This is an emergency summons. 
Briefing in 15 minutes.</i>

00:08:13.800 --> 00:08:15.050
<i>I'll be waiting.</i>

00:08:15.310 --> 00:08:17.360
Hey! You can't just...

00:08:17.750 --> 00:08:21.410
So once we're done shopping, there's 
this spot called Kibagata Park.

00:08:21.410 --> 00:08:24.890
It's a little far, but do you want to go?

00:08:25.300 --> 00:08:28.170
You can rent boats! 
It sounds like a lot of fun.

00:08:28.170 --> 00:08:30.860
Sorry, Minghua. I've gotta run.

00:08:32.060 --> 00:08:33.950
You can get me something next time.

00:08:33.950 --> 00:08:35.620
I'll think about what I want.

00:08:35.620 --> 00:08:36.980
Wai—

00:08:41.350 --> 00:08:43.490
What's your problem?

00:08:43.990 --> 00:08:46.180
Today at 0630,

00:08:46.180 --> 00:08:50.380
the Xi entered our ADIZ on the southwest 
side of the East China Sea.

00:08:50.380 --> 00:08:53.890
The JSDF and USAF scrambled immediately,

00:08:53.890 --> 00:08:57.110
but both suffered heavy damage 
and failed to defeat the enemy.

00:08:57.370 --> 00:09:02.770
The remaining enemy forces are circling an 
area 150 kilometers north of Ishigaki Island.

00:09:02.770 --> 00:09:07.050
Some of them have gone to Umidori 
Island, an uninhabited island nearby.

00:09:07.810 --> 00:09:09.150
Photo: Japan Coast Guard

00:09:09.140 --> 00:09:11.390
What is that?

00:09:11.390 --> 00:09:13.490
It may look bizarre,

00:09:13.490 --> 00:09:18.230
but from our analyses, 
this appears to be their FOB.

00:09:18.240 --> 00:09:18.910
Photo: Japan Coast Guard

00:09:18.800 --> 00:09:20.700
Their forward operating base.

00:09:21.170 --> 00:09:22.450
Forward operating base?

00:09:23.160 --> 00:09:24.910
Photo: Japan Coast Guard

00:09:25.040 --> 00:09:25.870
Photo: Japan Coast Guard

00:09:26.000 --> 00:09:26.670
Photo: Japan Coast Guard

00:09:26.790 --> 00:09:27.420
Photo: Japan Coast Guard

00:09:27.540 --> 00:09:28.170
Photo: Japan Coast Guard

00:09:28.290 --> 00:09:29.750
Photo: Japan Coast Guard

00:09:29.740 --> 00:09:33.270
After reaching Umidori Island,

00:09:33.270 --> 00:09:35.630
the Xi automatically deployed their cargo,

00:09:35.630 --> 00:09:37.680
which is transforming into a base,

00:09:38.120 --> 00:09:39.710
most likely.

00:09:39.710 --> 00:09:42.280
What happens when it's done transforming?

00:09:42.280 --> 00:09:45.220
Well, it would be a disaster, 
to put it mildly.

00:09:46.470 --> 00:09:48.760
This is the First Island Chain.

00:09:48.760 --> 00:09:51.620
The Far East's defense line against the Xi.

00:09:52.220 --> 00:09:55.230
And this is where they've landed.

00:09:57.050 --> 00:09:59.560
If they can maintain a presence here,

00:09:59.560 --> 00:10:02.010
the East China Sea defense 
line will collapse.

00:10:03.610 --> 00:10:05.100
What do we do?

00:10:05.530 --> 00:10:08.010
Destroy the base before it's finished.

00:10:08.010 --> 00:10:09.390
What else?

00:10:09.390 --> 00:10:12.090
So we just go blow it up?

00:10:12.090 --> 00:10:15.150
It's not that easy.

00:10:15.850 --> 00:10:18.470
We're not bombers.

00:10:18.470 --> 00:10:20.450
Even if we carried all the bombs we could,

00:10:20.450 --> 00:10:23.170
there's a limit to how much firepower we 
could bring to bear against a ground target.

00:10:23.170 --> 00:10:27.410
We wouldn't be able to neutralize 
the enemy's presence on the island.

00:10:27.870 --> 00:10:28.890
Correct.

00:10:29.370 --> 00:10:32.520
Thus, the US military and the 
JGSDF will attack the base.

00:10:35.010 --> 00:10:37.970
The remaining ships of 
the 7th Fleet, as well as

00:10:37.970 --> 00:10:41.080
the JGSDF forces on Ishigaki Island, 
will saturate the island with missiles.

00:10:41.930 --> 00:10:46.780
One hundred SSMs. About 50 tons of explosives
 will burn everything on that island to ash.

00:10:46.780 --> 00:10:48.940
But they have their EPCM.

00:10:48.940 --> 00:10:51.750
Normal weapons won't reach the target.

00:10:52.010 --> 00:10:55.900
Hence, the Daughters will take over guidance 
while the missiles are in flight.

00:10:55.900 --> 00:10:57.930
This operation will require you to run

00:10:57.930 --> 00:11:01.730
an air superiority mission while providing 
targeting support against all targets.

00:11:02.610 --> 00:11:06.680
Given the processing power required, we're 
going to have Phantom handle the guidance.

00:11:06.680 --> 00:11:08.640
The other two will provide escort.

00:11:11.430 --> 00:11:12.600
Escort?

00:11:13.150 --> 00:11:16.310
You're telling me to entrust 
these two with my life?

00:11:16.310 --> 00:11:17.460
Yes.

00:11:17.460 --> 00:11:19.240
Is that a problem?

00:11:21.340 --> 00:11:22.500
Hey...

00:11:24.280 --> 00:11:25.780
I refuse.

00:11:26.690 --> 00:11:29.150
I don't want to die for nothing.

00:11:29.150 --> 00:11:33.460
Hey, are you saying you don't 
trust me to escort you?

00:11:33.460 --> 00:11:37.100
But this entire operation depends 
on your processing power.

00:11:37.100 --> 00:11:39.980
You know nobody can do it but you.

00:11:43.150 --> 00:11:47.560
Then may I be placed in charge 
when we're in flight?

00:11:47.560 --> 00:11:51.430
If I'm allowed to change our mission 
parameters in response to the situation,

00:11:51.430 --> 00:11:52.720
I'll consider it.

00:11:56.400 --> 00:11:58.980
No way! No way! No way!

00:11:59.340 --> 00:12:02.400
Who does she think she is? Just because 
she won one single mock battle!

00:12:02.400 --> 00:12:04.900
That brat! Brat! Brat!

00:12:04.900 --> 00:12:06.030
Calm down.

00:12:06.030 --> 00:12:07.860
If you're that upset, 
you'll get in an accident.

00:12:14.140 --> 00:12:16.370
Kei, Haruka wants you to hurry up.

00:12:16.370 --> 00:12:17.930
He says to get your butt out there.

00:12:17.930 --> 00:12:19.330
Did something happen?

00:12:19.630 --> 00:12:22.400
Word came in from recon 
planes in the mission area.

00:12:22.400 --> 00:12:25.790
Additional transport-type Xi arrived 
and dropped more containers.

00:12:25.790 --> 00:12:29.960
Additional escorts have arrived, 
and it's getting difficult to get close.

00:12:29.960 --> 00:12:31.060
Let's hurry.

00:12:38.030 --> 00:12:40.740
<i>Barbie 03, contact departure.</i>

00:13:05.070 --> 00:13:08.130
Barbie 01, cleared for take off!

00:13:14.160 --> 00:13:16.510
After refueling mid-air at Cape Muroto,

00:13:16.510 --> 00:13:18.140
you'll head for the mission area.

00:13:18.410 --> 00:13:21.610
Eagle and Gripen are to bring down 
as many enemies as possible.

00:13:21.610 --> 00:13:23.770
Phantom is to enter the island's airspace,

00:13:24.050 --> 00:13:26.060
and as soon as the data link is established,

00:13:26.060 --> 00:13:28.630
give the launch order to the 
JGSDF and American militaries.

00:13:28.630 --> 00:13:29.360
Got it?

00:13:29.360 --> 00:13:30.730
02, roger!

00:13:30.730 --> 00:13:32.530
03, roger.

00:13:34.780 --> 00:13:38.780
Gripen... Can you open a 
channel just to Phantom?

00:13:38.780 --> 00:13:39.940
I can. Why?

00:13:39.940 --> 00:13:42.440
Can you let me talk to her for a second?

00:13:42.440 --> 00:13:44.580
Something feels wrong.

00:13:47.020 --> 00:13:49.520
<i>01 to 03. Do you read?</i>

00:13:50.190 --> 00:13:53.420
<i>What is it? Why do you need 
to use encrypted comms?</i>

00:13:53.740 --> 00:13:55.520
<i>Kei wants to talk to you.</i>

00:13:55.520 --> 00:13:56.880
<i>Passing the mic to him.</i>

00:14:00.370 --> 00:14:01.790
Is that you, Phantom?

00:14:01.790 --> 00:14:04.510
<i>Yes. Do you need something?</i>

00:14:04.510 --> 00:14:06.900
I heard from Yashirodoori-san.

00:14:06.900 --> 00:14:12.440
Um, you're trying your best to be useful 
to humans in your own way, right?

00:14:13.390 --> 00:14:17.310
We need to do something about this base...

00:14:17.650 --> 00:14:20.250
<i>What happens if we don't?</i>

00:14:21.720 --> 00:14:24.390
Humanity's total population is 7.5 billion.

00:14:24.390 --> 00:14:27.680
Japan's population, however, 
is a mere 120 million.

00:14:27.680 --> 00:14:29.590
Just 1.6% of humanity.

00:14:30.460 --> 00:14:32.580
<i>Even if everyone on the island chain dies,</i>

00:14:32.580 --> 00:14:35.200
<i>it's a small loss from the 
perspective of the larger whole.</i>

00:14:35.650 --> 00:14:38.110
You're willing to let Japan be destroyed?

00:14:38.110 --> 00:14:41.840
I cannot allow myself to die here.

00:14:42.250 --> 00:14:46.560
There are many enemies, 
and few Anima to deal with them.

00:14:47.010 --> 00:14:51.280
I absolutely need to live for as
 long as I can and destroy the Xi.

00:14:51.680 --> 00:14:55.680
<i>That is my reason d'être, 
the reason I was born.</i>

00:14:57.020 --> 00:14:59.410
The original Anima, like myself,

00:14:59.410 --> 00:15:02.710
underwent a rather roundabout 
method of development.

00:15:03.420 --> 00:15:06.470
We were forced to undergo 
countless simulations.

00:15:07.010 --> 00:15:09.690
We were forced to undergo different lives,
 under different conditions

00:15:09.690 --> 00:15:13.510
and for differing lengths, 
billions if not trillions of times.

00:15:13.880 --> 00:15:20.120
In terms of how much time I experienced, 
I'd say it was about a century.

00:15:20.120 --> 00:15:21.380
<i>A century?</i>

00:15:29.440 --> 00:15:32.170
It was quite difficult, you know.

00:15:32.170 --> 00:15:33.650
Immediately after birth,

00:15:33.650 --> 00:15:37.880
I didn't even know how to smile.

00:15:38.730 --> 00:15:44.530
Thanks to that, I was able to get more 
combat experience than the other Anima.

00:15:44.960 --> 00:15:49.570
I was able to make full use of my abilities 
and knowledge to complete my mission.

00:15:50.100 --> 00:15:53.060
I always have been, and I always will be,

00:15:53.760 --> 00:15:56.470
right up until the very last moment.

00:15:59.900 --> 00:16:01.590
<i>Don't worry.</i>

00:16:01.590 --> 00:16:06.680
<i>If Eagle and Gripen can do their jobs,
 I'll follow the plan.</i>

00:16:06.680 --> 00:16:08.490
O-Okay.

00:16:09.230 --> 00:16:10.960
<i>I'm returning to my checklist.</i>

00:16:10.960 --> 00:16:12.860
<i>Have a pleasant day.</i>

00:16:14.270 --> 00:16:16.770
Done talking?

00:16:17.160 --> 00:16:18.050
Yes.

00:16:25.170 --> 00:16:27.630
<i>Umidori Island</i>

00:16:28.140 --> 00:16:30.840
EPCM level rising.

00:16:30.840 --> 00:16:32.460
Gust 24,

00:16:32.460 --> 00:16:33.720
25,

00:16:33.720 --> 00:16:35.040
26...

00:16:35.390 --> 00:16:36.830
It's still rising.

00:16:36.830 --> 00:16:38.040
29,

00:16:38.040 --> 00:16:39.090
30...

00:16:39.400 --> 00:16:40.670
Deploying shields.

00:16:40.670 --> 00:16:42.010
Master arm, on.

00:16:43.390 --> 00:16:45.210
Kei, are you okay?

00:16:45.210 --> 00:16:46.920
Your heartbeat is unsteady.

00:16:46.920 --> 00:16:48.670
As are your breathing and pulse.

00:16:49.080 --> 00:16:52.040
I'm fine. Don't worry about it.

00:16:53.780 --> 00:16:56.130
Barbie 01, engage.

00:17:09.560 --> 00:17:11.460
Yahoo!

00:17:11.830 --> 00:17:13.640
She hit one with that?

00:17:28.500 --> 00:17:30.390
New enemies approaching.

00:17:30.390 --> 00:17:33.010
Radar contact. Four...

00:17:33.010 --> 00:17:34.690
No, eight of them.

00:17:36.500 --> 00:17:38.650
How much firepower do we have left?

00:17:38.650 --> 00:17:40.470
Eight AAMs.

00:17:40.470 --> 00:17:43.560
Eagle has 10 left, so 18 total.

00:17:43.560 --> 00:17:44.920
That and our machine guns.

00:17:45.390 --> 00:17:46.930
Where is Phantom?

00:17:46.930 --> 00:17:49.450
She needs to get into position 
and give the attack order.

00:17:51.340 --> 00:17:53.140
<i>Hey, get over here!</i>

00:17:53.140 --> 00:17:55.800
<i>We made you an opening!</i>

00:17:56.160 --> 00:17:56.800
Above.

00:18:00.570 --> 00:18:03.970
<i>If the enemy is using EMCON,
you're not going to get a warning.</i>

00:18:04.260 --> 00:18:06.830
<i>And if they get between you and the sun, 
visual identification is difficult.</i>

00:18:06.830 --> 00:18:09.770
<i>Striking from a blind spot is the 
traditional way to do a dogfight, right?</i>

00:18:17.080 --> 00:18:18.450
Oh, jeez!

00:18:18.820 --> 00:18:21.110
Just get over here!

00:18:21.110 --> 00:18:23.360
I'm running out of missiles!

00:18:23.360 --> 00:18:26.440
<i>You seem to be fully occupied 
protecting yourself.</i>

00:18:26.440 --> 00:18:28.880
<i>Can you also protect me?</i>

00:18:28.880 --> 00:18:31.600
It's not whether I <i>can</i> do it, I <i>am</i> doing it!

00:18:31.600 --> 00:18:32.840
Just follow the plan!

00:18:33.830 --> 00:18:34.940
Eagle!

00:18:34.940 --> 00:18:35.870
No!

00:18:41.390 --> 00:18:43.100
What is this?

00:18:46.310 --> 00:18:48.020
<i>Take this, dang it!</i>

00:18:51.740 --> 00:18:54.080
Limits reached. We should withdraw.

00:18:54.080 --> 00:18:55.980
<i>No way! Not when we're this close!</i>

00:18:56.300 --> 00:18:58.520
<i>If we run out of ammo, it will be too late.</i>

00:18:58.520 --> 00:18:59.800
<i>We won't be able to flee.</i>

00:19:04.570 --> 00:19:06.050
Gripen, Eagle, below us!

00:19:16.660 --> 00:19:18.230
What the hell was that?

00:19:18.230 --> 00:19:21.060
An SAM. A cluster bomb...

00:19:21.060 --> 00:19:22.880
Gripen, are you okay?

00:19:22.880 --> 00:19:24.790
It's the type launched from the ground.

00:19:24.790 --> 00:19:26.500
Probably a new weapon.

00:19:26.860 --> 00:19:28.110
<i>More are coming!</i>

00:19:29.010 --> 00:19:31.350
Retreat! Eagle, get out 
of here at full speed!

00:19:37.390 --> 00:19:38.740
No way!

00:19:39.520 --> 00:19:40.650
No way!

00:19:40.650 --> 00:19:43.300
We can't win like this.

00:19:47.410 --> 00:19:50.750
<i>Naha Base</i>

00:19:48.230 --> 00:19:50.750
Why didn't you do what Daddy told you to?

00:19:51.210 --> 00:19:53.820
Because you two can't be 
trusted to do your jobs.

00:19:53.820 --> 00:19:56.480
If you'd managed to achieve air superiority,

00:19:56.480 --> 00:19:59.180
I would've followed the plan.

00:19:59.180 --> 00:20:01.560
We can't take down that base like that!

00:20:01.560 --> 00:20:02.700
What do we do?

00:20:02.700 --> 00:20:05.890
Without enough combat power, 
there's nothing we can do.

00:20:06.420 --> 00:20:11.400
Why not ask the US or Russian 
military for additional Anima?

00:20:11.400 --> 00:20:13.370
And if they can't send any?

00:20:13.370 --> 00:20:16.640
We just abandon this area.

00:20:16.640 --> 00:20:19.990
You're certainly pessimistic, aren't you?

00:20:19.990 --> 00:20:21.990
Basically, you don't want to die, right?

00:20:22.540 --> 00:20:25.190
A weapon that chooses the battlefields 
it wants to fight on?

00:20:25.190 --> 00:20:26.670
That's pretty pathetic.

00:20:27.100 --> 00:20:28.750
K-Kei?

00:20:29.030 --> 00:20:31.250
That's a cheap provocation.

00:20:31.250 --> 00:20:34.960
Did you think you could 
provoke me into helping?

00:20:34.960 --> 00:20:37.520
Provoke you? Don't be stupid.

00:20:37.940 --> 00:20:39.840
I'm simply telling the truth.

00:20:39.840 --> 00:20:44.680
Those enemies were nothing compared 
to the attack on Komatsu.

00:20:45.110 --> 00:20:46.340
Right, Gripen?

00:20:46.780 --> 00:20:49.840
You shot down more Xi than that 
during that battle, right?

00:20:51.840 --> 00:20:54.440
This is nothing? Of course it's nothing.

00:20:54.440 --> 00:20:57.640
These guys were chumps.

00:20:58.040 --> 00:21:01.230
It's ridiculous that Phantom 
is afraid of them.

00:21:01.870 --> 00:21:03.490
No, that's not right.

00:21:03.490 --> 00:21:05.250
She's just weak.

00:21:05.250 --> 00:21:07.820
So weak she can't win unless she catches 
you off-guard in a mock battle.

00:21:08.140 --> 00:21:10.450
That's a very funny joke.

00:21:10.830 --> 00:21:14.050
You think she could beat 
me in a straight-up fight?

00:21:14.050 --> 00:21:16.340
With her unstable, light airframe,

00:21:16.340 --> 00:21:19.240
and carrying fragile cargo like you?

00:21:19.570 --> 00:21:23.610
Of course. A coward like you 
wouldn't last an instant.

00:21:23.610 --> 00:21:25.270
That's what she says.

00:21:26.090 --> 00:21:28.750
Let's make it clear who's right.

00:21:29.290 --> 00:21:31.880
If we win, you're going to 
change the way you act.

00:21:32.290 --> 00:21:35.610
You're the new girl, and you're 
going to start listening to orders.

00:21:35.610 --> 00:21:41.930
And if I win, you'll do whatever I tell you?

00:21:41.930 --> 00:21:43.060
Hm...

00:21:43.790 --> 00:21:49.070
Then I'll ask you to leave Gripen 
and be my partner instead, maybe.

00:21:50.030 --> 00:21:51.010
Very well.

00:23:27.810 --> 00:23:30.310
Next time on <i>Girly Air Force</i>...

00:23:30.310 --> 00:23:33.440
ALT 07: "After the Bewilderment."

00:23:30.550 --> 00:23:40.010
<i>After the Bewilderment</i>

00:23:33.880 --> 00:23:37.580
Barbie 01, cleared for take off!
